'''''Marvel's Spider-Man''''' is an American [[animated series|animated television series]], based on the [[Spider-Man|Marvel Comics character of the same name]]. A replacement for the previous series ''[[Ultimate Spider-Man (TV series)|Ultimate Spider-Man]]'', the first season premiered on August 19, 2017, on [[Disney XD]].<ref name=ew/><ref name="ut"/> The show was subtitled '''''Maximum Venom''''' for its third season,<ref name="S3" /> which premiered on April 19, 2020.<ref name="Maximum Venom"/>
{{TOC limit|3}}

== Plot ==
=== Season 1 ===
Gifted teenager [[Peter Parker]] is given superpowers when he is bitten by a radioactive spider during a school field trip to [[Oscorp]] Industries. After the death of his [[Uncle Ben]] by a [[Burglar (comics)|burglar]] that he hesitated to stop at a wrestling arena, Peter comes to his own terms of being the superhero Spider-Man. Sometime later, Peter begins learning how to balance his crime-fighting career with his new enrollment at Horizon High, a school for students with genius-level intellect run by [[Max Modell]]. Joining Peter in his ordeals against [[Norman Osborn]], [[Jackal (Marvel Comics character)|Jackal]], and numerous other villains are his classmates [[Gwen Stacy]], [[Miles Morales]] (who develops powers similar to Peter's and becomes the Ultimate Spider-Man), and [[Anya Corazon]], as well as his best friend [[Harry Osborn]] (who eventually becomes the superhero [[Hobgoblin (Marvel Comics)|Hobgoblin]]).<ref name="ew">{{cite magazine |last=Holub |first=Christian |date=June 28, 2017 |title=Revisit Spider-Man's origin in new animated short |url=http://ew.com/tv/2017/06/28/spider-man-origin-animated-short-exclusive/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171014125640/http://ew.com/tv/2017/06/28/spider-man-origin-animated-short-exclusive/ |archive-date=October 14, 2017 |access-date=July 14, 2017 |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]}}</ref>

Besides Norman and Jackal, other villains introduced this season include [[Doctor Octopus]], [[Vulture (Marvel Comics)|Vulture]], [[Venom (character)|Venom]], [[Rhino (character)|Rhino]], [[Spencer Smythe|Spencer]] and [[Alistair Smythe]], [[Kraven the Hunter]], [[Black Cat (Marvel Comics)|Black Cat]], [[Advanced Idea Mechanics|A.I.M.]], [[Lizard (character)|Curt Connors]], [[Keemia Alvarado|Sandgirl]], [[Mac Gargan|Scorpion]], and [[Crossbones (character)|Crossbones]]. Other characters introduced in this season include [[Aunt May|May Parker]], [[Flash Thompson]], [[Liz Allan]], [[Randy Robertson (character)|Randy Robertson]], [[Robbie Robertson (character)|Robbie Robertson]], [[Iron Man]], [[Hulk]], [[Black Widow (Natasha Romanova)|Black Widow]], and [[Sandman (Marvel Comics)|Sandman]].

=== Season 2 ===
Taking place a few months after the previous season, Otto Octavius possesses Spider-Man's body and becomes the [[The Superior Spider-Man|Superior Spider-Man]]. Peter's consciousness transfers into Otto's tentacle harness and convinces him to reverse the swap. Towards the end of the season, Spider-Man and company discover the existence of a cult-like organization led by Adrian Toomes as the [[Goblin King]].<ref>{{cite web |last=Cecchini |first=Mike |date=January 25, 2018 |title=Spider-Man Season 2 Will Follow the Superior Spider-Man Story |url=http://www.denofgeek.com/us/tv/spider-man/270484/spider-man-season-2-will-follow-the-superior-spider-man-story |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181001200648/http://www.denofgeek.com/us/tv/spider-man/270484/spider-man-season-2-will-follow-the-superior-spider-man-story |archive-date=October 1, 2018 |access-date=January 3, 2019 |work=[[Den of Geek]]}}</ref>

During this season, Peter gains a career at the ''[[Daily Bugle]]'', Anya becomes Spider-Girl after gaining superpowers from the "[[Spider-Island]]" incident, Gwen becomes [[Spider-Woman (Gwen Stacy)|Ghost-Spider]] after gaining superpowers from the Blood Gem, and Spider-Man forms a "Spider Team" with his inner circle.

This season introduces more villains, including [[Chameleon (character)|Chameleon]], [[Electro (Marvel Comics)|Electro]], [[Silvermane]], [[Regent (comics)|Regent]], [[Abner Jenkins|Beetle]], [[Silver Sable]], [[Tinkerer (Marvel Comics)|Tinkerer]], [[Monica Rappaccini]], [[MODOK]], [[Slyde]], [[Eddie Brock]], and the [[Vulturions|Wake Riders]]. Other characters introduced in this season include [[Anna Maria Marconi]], [[Cloak and Dagger (characters)|Cloak and Dagger]], [[Kamala Khan|Ms. Marvel]], [[Wraith (Yuri Watanabe)|Yuri Watanabe]], [[Prowler (Marvel Comics)|Prowler]], [[Black Tiger (comics)|Abraham Brown]], [[Captain America]], [[J. Jonah Jameson]], [[Grady Scraps]], [[Carol Danvers|Captain Marvel]], and original character Nocturnal.

=== Season 3 (''Maximum Venom'') ===
Taking place two weeks after the previous season, Spider-Man uncovers two separate plots centered on Venom. The most prominent is helping Max Modell save the Earth from an invasion of [[Symbiote (comics)|Klyntar]] summoned by Venom. The secondary plot is a conspiracy helmed by Curt Connors to frame Modell for Venom's actions. Backed up by Hobgoblin, the Spider Team exposes Norman's conspiracy, resulting in Modell regaining his job. During the battle with the Klyntar, Horizon High is destroyed, with the Spiders planning to build a tech laboratory called the Worldwide Engineering Brigade to replace it.

Besides Dark Goblin, other villains introduced in this season include [[Scream (character)|Scream]], [[Scorn (Marvel Comics)|Scorn]], [[Mania (character)|Mania]], [[Swarm (Marvel Comics)|Swarm]] ([[Jefferson Davis (character)|Jefferson Davis]]), [[Tarantula (Marvel Comics)|Tarantula]], [[Baron Mordo]], and the Klyntar dragon [[Grendel (Marvel Comics)|Grendel]]. Other characters introduced in this season include [[Ironheart (character)|Ironheart]], the [[Amadeus Cho|Totally Awesome Hulk]], [[Doctor Strange]], [[Star-Lord]], [[Groot]], [[Moon Knight]], [[Anti-Venom]], and [[Thor (Marvel Comics)|Thor]].

